# NCD Test Suite Quality Remediation Plan

Date: 2026-05-08
Scope: `test/` C tests, test harness scripts, and test utility code
Objective: make the test suite deterministic, DRY, platform-abstracted, and trustworthy for staff-level engineering quality.

---

## Audit Method

1. Full repository scan of tracked `test/` sources and scripts.
2. Pattern analysis for skip behavior, dead code, duplicated helpers, platform conditionals, and fragile command execution.
3. Targeted manual review of high-risk files.

---

## Core Quality Rules (Required)

1. A skipped test is never counted as passed.
2. Platform branching belongs in shared test helpers, not repeated in every test file.
3. Service/process orchestration helpers must be centralized and reused.
4. Shell command construction must be quoted/escaped and path-safe.
5. Sleep-based synchronization should be replaced with bounded condition polling whenever possible.

---

## Priority Legend

- T0: correctness risk in test verdicts or regression coverage (fix first)
- T1: high-value DRY/platform/bug-risk cleanup
- T2: maintainability and readability improvements
- T3: nice-to-have quality polish

---

## T0 - Correctness / Trustworthiness

### T0.1 - Skip-as-pass semantics in C test framework
- Evidence:
  - `test/test_framework.h:79-89` (`RUN_TEST`) treats any `test_*() == 0` as PASSED.
  - Many tests print `SKIP:` then `return 0;` (examples: `test/test_service_rescan.c:130`, `test/test_service_integration.c:628`).
- Risk: false-green test runs with missing executable/runtime prerequisites.
- Fix:
  - Add explicit skip signaling to framework (`TEST_SKIP()` macro and `tests_skipped` counter).
  - Update `RUN_TEST` to classify PASS/FAIL/SKIP distinctly.
  - Fail suite if required test classes are skipped unexpectedly.
- Required tests:
  - New `test/test_framework_contract.c` validating PASS/FAIL/SKIP accounting.

### T0.2 - P0.1 regression test is missing from suite
- Evidence:
  - `test/test_service_database.c` currently has no `regression_rescan_no_data_loss` test.
  - Main remediation plan previously referenced this test as existing.
- Risk: known service rescan data-loss path is not guarded by regression coverage.
- Fix:
  - Add `TEST(regression_rescan_no_data_loss)` in `test/test_service_database.c`.
  - Gate with `NCD_ENABLE_KNOWN_BUG_TESTS=1` until fixed; then enforce always-on.
- Required tests:
  - Red baseline with known-bug mode enabled, then green post-fix.

### T0.3 - Dead disabled test block in source (`#if 0` nested)
- Evidence:
  - `test/test_service_integration.c:656-682` has nested `#if 0` around a full test.
- Risk: dead code rots and silently diverges from behavior expectations.
- Fix:
  - Either delete block or convert to active test with proper registration and guards.
- Required tests:
  - If re-enabled, ensure it runs under harness and fails meaningfully when behavior regresses.

---

## T1 - DRY, Platform Boundaries, and Potential Bugs

### T1.1 - Service helper logic duplicated across 10+ files
- Evidence (representative):
  - `test/test_service_integration.c:106` (`run_service_command`)
  - `test/test_service_lifecycle.c:70`
  - `test/test_service_ipc.c:77`
  - `test/test_service_rescan.c:54`
  - `test/test_service_stress.c:62`
  - Similar duplication for `service_executable_exists`, `ensure_service_stopped`, `wait_for_service_state`, `force_terminate_service`.
- Risk: behavioral drift, inconsistent timeouts, and repeated bugs.
- Fix:
  - Create `test/service_test_common.h/.c` and migrate all service tests to it.
  - Centralize start/stop/wait/process-check logic.
- Required tests:
  - New unit tests for helper contract (start-stop idempotency, timeout behavior).

### T1.2 - Agent integration helper duplication across test files
- Evidence:
  - Repeated `get_temp_dir`, `rm_rf`, `find_exe`, `run_agent`, `create_test_db` across:
    - `test/test_agent_complete_mkdir_quit.c`
    - `test/test_agent_ls_check.c`
    - `test/test_agent_query_tree.c`
    - `test/test_agent_mv.c`
    - `test/test_agent_rmdir.c`
    - `test/test_agent_verify.c`
- Risk: bug fixes must be patched repeatedly; quoting/path rules diverge.
- Fix:
  - Create `test/agent_test_common.h/.c` and delete per-file clones.
- Required tests:
  - One helper-focused test binary validating temp-dir and executable-discovery behavior.

### T1.3 - Unquoted Windows command environment assignment (path with spaces bug)
- Evidence:
  - `test/test_agent_mv.c:106` and `test/test_agent_rmdir.c:93`: `set LOCALAPPDATA=%s&& ...`
- Risk: breaks in user profiles with spaces; potential command injection in test env strings.
- Fix:
  - Quote and sanitize env assignments (`set "LOCALAPPDATA=%s" && ...`).
- Required tests:
  - Add test case with temp path containing spaces.

### T1.4 - Process exit-status handling is unsafe on POSIX
- Evidence:
  - `return WEXITSTATUS(status);` without `WIFEXITED(status)` in multiple files:
    - `test/test_service_integration.c:101`
    - `test/test_service_lifecycle.c:132`
    - `test/test_service_ipc.c:146`
    - `test/test_service_rescan.c:98`
    - `test/test_service_stress.c:106`
    - and others.
- Risk: undefined/incorrect status reporting when child exits via signal.
- Fix:
  - Centralize decode helper (`normalize_exit_status`) and use everywhere.
- Required tests:
  - Simulated signaled child process case in helper tests.

### T1.5 - Large platform-specific conditional blocks in tests
- Evidence (examples):
  - `test/test_service_init_db.c:152-300` (`#if NCD_PLATFORM_WINDOWS`, span ~149 lines)
  - `test/test_service_stress.c:147-295` (span ~149 lines)
  - `test/test_service_ipc.c:192-340` (span ~149 lines)
  - `test/test_ipc_extended.c:130-234` (span ~105 lines)
- Risk: giant dual implementations reduce readability and increase platform drift.
- Fix:
  - Move platform specifics to helper APIs in `service_test_common` and `ipc_test_common`.
- Required tests:
  - Cross-platform parity checks that call shared helper APIs.

### T1.6 - Sleep-driven synchronization causes flakiness and slow tests
- Evidence:
  - High density of `platform_sleep_ms(...)` in service tests (`test_service_rescan.c`, `test_service_stress.c`, `test_service_race_conditions.c`, etc.).
- Risk: nondeterministic timing, longer runtime, occasional CI flakes.
- Fix:
  - Replace fixed sleeps with `wait_until(predicate, timeout, poll_interval)` helper.
  - Keep sleeps only where explicitly testing timing behavior.
- Required tests:
  - Helper tests proving timeout and wake behavior.

### T1.7 - Repeated shell-based recursive delete wrappers (`rm_rf`) in agent tests
- Evidence:
  - Repeated `system("rmdir /s /q ...")` and `system("rm -rf ...")` in 8+ files.
- Risk: command quoting risks and repeated shell dependence.
- Fix:
  - Replace with one safe helper in `agent_test_common` using platform wrappers where possible.
- Required tests:
  - Path with spaces and special chars deletion tests.

---

## T2 - Maintainability and Dead Code

### T2.1 - Unused static helper
- Evidence:
  - `test/test_agent_mkdir_extended.c:31` `get_temp_dir` appears unused.
- Risk: dead code and reader confusion.
- Fix:
  - Remove unused helper or use shared helper.

### T2.2 - Monolithic test files
- Evidence:
  - `test/service_race_tester.c` (~1281 lines)
  - `test/test_database.c` (~1138 lines)
  - `test/test_scanner_extended.c` (~1002 lines)
- Risk: difficult review/debug, high merge-conflict probability.
- Fix:
  - Split by domain and helper layer; keep each test file under ~500 lines when practical.

### T2.3 - Legacy disabled tests in Makefile comments
- Evidence:
  - `test/Makefile` comments show disabled agent tests (`test_agent_mkdir`, `test_mkdirs`) rather than explicit harness policy.
- Risk: stale intent and confusing coverage expectations.
- Fix:
  - Move disabled rationale into a single test manifest with owner and re-enable criteria.

---

## T3 - Polish

### T3.1 - Normalize test command wrappers and output formatting
- Standardize command execution helpers and logging format between `.bat`, `.sh`, and Python runner glue.

### T3.2 - Add test-health dashboard
- Generate summary metrics: skipped-by-reason, flaky retries, platform parity failures, and missing executable rates.

---

## Implementation Waves (Parallel-Friendly)

### Wave A (T0 first, blocking)
1. Add framework skip semantics and contract tests.
2. Restore/add `regression_rescan_no_data_loss`.
3. Remove/resolve `#if 0` dead test block.

### Wave B (shared helper extraction)
1. Build `service_test_common` and migrate service test files.
2. Build `agent_test_common` and migrate agent test files.
3. Add centralized exit-status normalize helper.

### Wave C (stability + platform cleanup)
1. Replace fixed sleeps with wait-until helper.
2. Shrink large `#if` blocks by moving logic into helper implementation files.
3. Fix Windows quoting and path handling in command construction.

### Wave D (maintainability)
1. Remove dead helpers.
2. Split monolithic test files.
3. Replace disabled-comment patterns with tracked manifest.

---

## DeepSeek Subagent Ownership Plan

1. Agent T-A (framework + harness)
   - Owns: `test/test_framework.h`, `test/test_framework.c`, `test/runner.py`, `test/ncd_testlib/executor.py`
   - Items: T0.1, parts of reporting semantics.
2. Agent T-B (service helper consolidation)
   - Owns: service-oriented test C files + new `test/service_test_common.*`
   - Items: T1.1, T1.4, T1.6.
3. Agent T-C (agent helper consolidation)
   - Owns: `test/test_agent_*.c` + new `test/agent_test_common.*`
   - Items: T1.2, T1.3, T1.7, T2.1.
4. Agent T-D (dead code / manifest / structure)
   - Owns: `test/Makefile`, integration test file cleanup, file splitting plan
   - Items: T0.3, T2.2, T2.3, T3.1.

Rules:
- Disjoint write scopes only.
- Every bug-risk item must include red->green evidence.
- Full integration run required after each wave.

---

## Completion Gate

- [ ] No skipped tests are reported as passed.
- [ ] All critical regression tests exist and are runnable via harness.
- [ ] Duplicated service/agent helpers replaced by shared utility modules.
- [ ] Platform `#if` blocks in test files reduced to thin wrappers.
- [ ] Command invocation and exit-status handling are safe and consistent.
- [ ] Full report (`python test/generate_report.py`) remains green with explicit skip accounting.
